  "evidence": [
    "Pinned vox_draw_scene639E60 stores descriptor14/18/1C at639EE0..639EFD to scratch+0C/+10/+14; stores descriptor0/4/8 at639F03..639F1F to scratch+4/+0/+8. Accessed window9BE6A4..9BE6BC is24bytes, three pointers(depth/colour/shadow) then three uint32 steps(colour/depth/shadow). This does not independently prove original aggregate class name, total allocation or larger parent ownership.",
    "Caviar init_class6185A0 populates CaviarScene.setup_; vox_create_record6393C0 borrows descriptor pointer; vox_draw_scene copies in original row-step-then-colour/depth/shadow order before setup callback. Caviar set_buffer6183D0 is not a descriptor producer and is outside this intent. Keep static shared scratch, overwrite order, borrowing and failure/reentrant behavior; no null/capacity guards or owning copies.",
    "Consumers in caviar_raster_kernels.inc216/580..599 and caviar.cpp4330 require depth-pitch units, colour pixel-size multiplication and shadow pitch unchanged. Preserve defined32bit numeric address differences separately; do not turn actual arithmetic scratch into pointers or invent array bounds. Keep callback/projection alias uncertainties and existing obligations.",
    "Native x86 compiler must independently verify 24byte current view, field offsets/widths and current global symbol before source object binding; host pointer width is not ABI proof. Start-only source binding may express proven original scratch start, but accessed24bytes alone grants no full original allocation/data extent claim. Preserve source-owned function identities and historical claims; coordinator owns compiler-proven symbol/object annotation publication. New host tests must extract actual descriptor-copy block, assert pointer identities before callback, pitches/overwrite order, and real raster destinations/mutants."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover the bounded per-draw six-word scratch as three borrowed output pointers plus three row steps, closing descriptor-copy and raster consumers without integer-pointer truncation or invented larger ownership.",
